\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\section{Introduction}
\label{sec:introduction}
Type systems catch errors early, but gradual typing adds runtime cost.
\section{Preliminaries}
\label{sec:preliminaries}
We assume familiarity with simply typed lambda calculus.
\section{Approach}
\label{sec:approach}
We insert checks only at module boundaries, guided by blame analysis.
\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
Boundary checks preserve most of the safety at a fraction of the cost. As Section~\ref{sec:approach} shows, confining checks to module boundaries is what makes this trade-off practical.
\end{document}
